for two weeks the greek island of zanti  with its crystal clear waters  provided the perfect escape for  stephanie whitfield and her husband  then came the flight home to cardiff on  tuesday  there wasn't much social distancing and  people didn't seem to be very well  educated in the use of wearing masks  we had people wearing it underneath  their noses underneath their chins  and people taking the mask off to talk  to other people  in fact they were so worried they'd  already decided to self-isolate  even before news emerged that 16  passengers on tui flight 6215  had tested positive for covid seven were  thought to be potentially infectious  while on the plane  tui says it's concerned to hear about  mrs whitfield's claims  and a full investigation is underway  making it clear that passengers are  informed both before  and during the flight of the need to  wear masks  except when eating and drinking now  there are questions about how long it's  taking health officials  to contact the 193 people on board  to tell them to self-isolate if ever  there was a case study  for why arrival testing at airports  needs to be introduced as soon as  possible  then this tui flight is it they could  have captured everybody coming off the  flight  immediately tested them then ask them to  quarantine for five days  and then do a second test and if that  process had been carried out  as other countries are doing then they  would have been able to contact  everybody straight away  many airlines have been strictly  enforcing the rules  but there's concern about whether those  rules are up to the job  if for say over 95 percent of the flight  time  everyone wore the mask properly then it  would be  some degree of additional protection  afforded to all the passengers and the  crew  on that airline on the other hand  if they are only wearing the mask for  about say  50 or less during the flight  then actually on a full flight it is  only  very symbolic and nobody is being  protected  in that case about 30 people returning  to wales from different parts of zante  on different planes have tested positive  for the virus in the past week  it's hard to tell when the passengers on  tuesday's flight were infected  now stephanie has developed a mild cough  and sore throat  she and her husband will be tested on  tuesday to see if they should be added  to that list  emma birchley sky news
 

